{# The header of a SCREEN: what this screen is, what can be done to it, and — on
   an entity place — which of its faces you are looking at. It fills
   `canvas.header`, and it owns the screen's single h1 (D5): every further
   heading on the screen is a `zone` heading and renders one level below it.

   THERE IS EXACTLY ONE h1 ELEMENT IN THIS TEMPLATE, not one per branch. The
   heading slot and the `title` prop are two ways of filling the same heading, so
   they resolve to one value before it is rendered; writing the element twice
   would make "the screen has one heading" a property of which branch happened to
   be taken rather than a property of this file.

   It exists because the add action belongs to the screen that can receive the
   addition, not to the shell's chrome
   (designbook/design-system/action-pattern.md).

   That is the whole reason this component was added rather than reusing
   something. A global "Add <entity>" button parked in the top bar is the Drupal
   toolbar mindset: the chrome cannot know whether the screen under it can accept
   an addition, so it either shows an action that sometimes lies or hides one that
   sometimes puzzles. Moving the affordance into the screen's own header makes the
   question answerable by the only component that knows — the screen.

   `actions` is right-aligned by this component rather than by whatever fills it,
   so every screen's actions land in the same place and a scene cannot drift.

   ABSENCE IS THE POINT of the `actions` slot. A screen that cannot add fills
   nothing and the affordance does not exist — it is not rendered disabled and not
   rendered hidden. A hidden control is still a promise the screen cannot keep,
   and a disabled one invites the operator to hunt for the condition that would
   enable it. Both are worse than nothing where the answer is "not here".

   THE TABS LIVE HERE, below the title row, rather than in a chrome component of
   their own (D7). Ant Design's `PageHeader` and Primer's `PageHeader.Navigation`
   both fold them in, and this component already carries the title, the sub-line
   and the actions — a second component whose only content is a header and a tab
   row would have nothing else to be. An entity place fills the slot; every other
   screen leaves it empty and renders exactly one row, as before.

   THE BREADCRUMB LIVES HERE TOO, above the title row and still inside this
   header, so a nested place can name its parents without a Drupal breadcrumb
   region. Empty is the supported case and renders no extra row.

   Spacing is the token scale, never a hard pixel value (D16). #}
<header{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass([
    'flex', 'flex-col', 'border-b', 'border-border-2', 'text-text',
  ]) }}
  data-page-header>
  {#- THE HEADING MAY BE THE FIELD. A screen that shows ONE object carries that
      object's name as its heading, and a name is a reversible field — so on the
      workspace screen the heading holds a `bb_theme:form_input` (BB-420
      Task 31; formerly the bespoke `text_line`) and the commit IS the write
      (action-pattern.md › *Inline edit*). The slot is captured outside the `if`,
      because a filled slot must render even when no `title` prop was passed; and
      it stays inside the heading element, because an editable heading is still
      the screen's heading and a text input contributes its value to the
      heading's accessible name. Every other screen fills nothing and the `title`
      prop renders exactly as before. #}
  {%- set heading_content %}{% block heading %}{{ heading }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
  {%- set breadcrumb_content %}{% block breadcrumb %}{{ breadcrumb }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
  {%- set tabs_content %}{% block tabs %}{{ tabs }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
  {%- set editable = heading_content|trim is not empty %}
  {%- if breadcrumb_content|trim is not empty %}
    <div class="px-card xl:px-gutter pt-card">{{ breadcrumb_content }}</div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-card min-h-11 px-card xl:px-gutter {{ breadcrumb_content|trim is not empty ? 'pb-card pt-inline' : 'py-card' }}">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-stack min-w-0">
      <div class="shrink-0 empty:hidden">{% block leading %}{{ leading }}{% endblock %}</div>
    <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
      {#- THE EDITABLE HEADING USED TO NEED HOVER/FOCUS STYLING TO LOOK EDITABLE,
          AND NO LONGER DOES (BB-420 Task 31). `text_line` was borderless by
          contract — that is the widget grammar, and it is right inside a create
          dialog where the operator came to type. On a READ screen a borderless
          field rendered pixel-identical to static heading text, so a hover/focus
          reveal (targeting the retired `text_line` component's own styling hook) was applied HERE, by this
          caller, to disclose it. `text_line` is retired: every editable field is
          now `bb_theme:form_input`, which carries its own permanent visible
          border and background — the field looks like a field at rest, on every
          screen, with nothing left to disclose on hover. The class hook and its
          selectors are removed rather than re-targeted at `form_input`'s own
          classes, since re-adding a reveal for an already-visible border would be
          a new visual decision, not a swap; report to the operator if the heading
          is judged to want one. #}
      {%- set editable_classes = 'min-w-0' %}
      {%- if editable or title %}
        <h1 class="text-page-title font-display font-bold text-title {{ editable ? editable_classes : 'truncate' }}"{% if not editable %} title="{{ title }}"{% endif %}>{{ editable ? heading_content : title }}</h1>
      {% endif %}
      {%- if description %}
        {#- One page header per page: the fixed id lets an htmx swap refresh the line out of band. #}
        {#- A clipped line keeps its full text in the tooltip. #}
        <p id="page-header-description" class="truncate text-meta text-text-faint" title="{{ description }}">{{ description }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    </div>
    {#- `justify-between` on the row rather than an auto-margin utility on this
        element — an outer margin belongs to a layout component, not to this
        content one — so a header with no title still pushes its actions to the
        right edge. #}
    <div class="flex items-center gap-stack shrink-0">
      {%- block actions %}{% if actions %}{{ actions }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {#- The tab row sits BELOW the title row and ABOVE this header's bottom border,
      so the active tab reads as attached to the body it reveals. No bottom padding:
      the active tab's underline sits on that bottom rule. Absent on every screen
      that is not an entity place. #}
  {%- if tabs_content|trim is not empty %}
    <div class="px-card xl:px-gutter">{{ tabs_content }}</div>
  {% endif %}
</header>
